{
  "$comment": "Retro Arcade content rules. Each rule has an action (decision of Jack, 2026-10-02). \"block\" is for sexual content: a catalog must not list the title, the ROM proxy returns 404 for its ROM file, and the catalog generators do not upload it. \"notice\" is for mainstream violent classics: the title stays in the catalog with no label in the list, and the arcade shows a heads-up card each time a player opens it. When a title matches a block rule and a notice rule, the block rule applies. Each rule is a case-insensitive regular expression. src/games/retro-arcade/lib/content-rules.ts (the catalog test and the ROM proxy) and scripts/retro_content_rules.py (the catalog generators) read this file. The browser gets only the notice rules, from lib/content-notice.generated.ts. After you change a notice rule, run pnpm --filter web generate:content-notice. Write each pattern so that JavaScript and Python read it the same way. Match text is lowercase, with '_' and '-' changed to spaces. A rule is checked against the display name, the ROM file name without its extension, and the id. Put a title in safeTitles when it looks like a matched title but no rule may match it.",
